WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.553
Intrinsic motivation means doing something because the activity itself is interesting, meaningful, satisfying, or aligned with identity.

2
00:00:07.553 --> 00:00:15.994
A person might enjoy solving a problem, improving a craft, helping a team, or understanding a system more deeply.

3
00:00:15.994 --> 00:00:22.658
Intrinsic motivation is valuable because it can support persistence even when external pressure is low.

4
00:00:22.658 --> 00:00:31.099
Extrinsic motivation means doing something for an external outcome, such as pay, recognition, status, deadlines, requirements, rewards, or consequences.

5
00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:33.764
Extrinsic motivation is not automatically bad.

6
00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:35.986
Deadlines can help people prioritize.

7
00:00:35.986 --> 00:00:38.207
Recognition can reinforce valuable work.

8
00:00:38.207 --> 00:00:41.761
Rewards can focus attention on an important behavior.

9
00:00:41.761 --> 00:00:45.760
External structures are part of how organizations coordinate effort.

10
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.202
The risk is that poorly designed incentives can distort behavior.

11
00:00:50.202 --> 00:00:55.534
If the reward system celebrates speed but ignores quality, people may rush.

12
00:00:55.534 --> 00:01:00.421
If metrics count activity but not outcomes, people may produce noise.

13
00:01:00.421 --> 00:01:05.752
If status comes from visible heroics, teams may neglect boring prevention work.

14
00:01:05.752 --> 00:01:14.193
Rewards should be aligned with real quality, long-term performance, and the behaviors the organization actually wants to see.

15
00:01:14.193 --> 00:01:18.191
A practical approach is to combine motivation sources thoughtfully.

16
00:01:18.191 --> 00:01:29.298
Make the work meaningful where possible, give people enough autonomy to own their effort, and use external incentives to support rather than corrupt the goal.

17
00:01:29.298 --> 00:01:35.518
The question is not whether intrinsic or extrinsic motivation is better in every case.

18
00:01:35.518 --> 00:01:43.071
The question is whether the motivation system encourages the right behavior for the right reasons over time.
